Author: ed3c <ed3c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 1 15:54:33 2026 +0800

    feat(maintain): split the loop into a reader-only SHADOW half and a proposing BUILD half
    
    The BUILD half existed only as pinned pstack procedure bytes plus
    adjudication comments on ed3c/skill-concerns#59: nothing went red when an
    agent edited a skill directory inline and called it maintenance. Both halves
    now have carriers at the shared exit.
    
    SHADOW stays the default and keeps having no write verb; its edit-scope
    digest now names the paths that moved instead of always blaming
    registry.json, and a planted repository gate that writes into skills/ is the
    negative control proving the refusal can fire.
    
    BUILD is --pass SKILL: it creates maintain/<skill>-<stamp>, regenerates
    through the subject Skill's own gen_*.py producers, and commits only under
    skills/<skill>/. The guard is git status after every producer, so one
    out-of-scope path refuses the producer, restores the tree, and blocks the
    pass; a planted producer writing into policy/ is that negative control. The
    base branch head is re-read and asserted unchanged before the pass exits.
    
    check_skill_bundles gains scan_role_declarations: a Skill claiming BUILD or
    SHADOW must declare both in one Roles block, with the reader-only clause and
    the S0/S1/S2 severities, or the gate reds.
    
    The three sc#59 adjudications - runtime/ceremony boundary, filing-not-reflex
    coupling, trigger-not-apply exception - are now tree bytes in AGENTS.md with
    a test that reds if one is deleted.
    
    Refs ed3c/skill-concerns#62
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
